Logic :

  Insert the element in that correct position
  keep sorting each subarray i.e., [1] [1,2] [1,2,3] ... [1,...,n]
  for each pass , the element inserted in that correct position
  Intuition : whenever the element is less than its previous element , break the loop , which indicates that the element inserted in that correct position. Otherwise , swap the element

Example :

  arr=[5,3,4,1,2]
  i -> 0 : 5 3 4 1 2
  i -> 1 : 3 5 4 1 2
  i -> 2 : 3 4 5 1 2
  i -> 3 : 1 3 4 5 2
  i -> 4 : 1 2 3 4 5

Code :

  static void insertionsort(int[] arr){
	    if(arr.length==1){
	        return;
	    }
	    for(int i=0;i<arr.length-1;i++){
	        for(int j=i+1;j>0;j--){
	            if(arr[j]>arr[j-1]){
	                break;
	            }
	            int temp=arr[j];
	            arr[j]=arr[j-1];
	            arr[j-1]=temp;
	        }
	    }
	}


Complexity

Best case (already sorted): O(n) (because of the break)
Average case: O(n²)
Worst case (reverse sorted): O(n²)
Space complexity: O(1)
